        "routeSummary": "With Lachen and Lachung",
        "overviewText": "This **10 Days 9 Nights North Sikkim tour with [Lachen](https://indiatour.live/attractions/lachen) and Lachung** is a **complete Himalayan journey**, covering Gangtok, Lachen, Lachung, Pelling, and Darjeeling in one seamless itinerary.\n\nYour trip begins with a scenic transfer from Siliguri to [Gangtok](https://indiatour.live/attractions/gangtok), where you settle into the mountains before heading out for an excursion to **Tsomgo Lake** and Baba Mandir—one of the most iconic high-altitude experiences in Sikkim.\n\nFrom Gangtok, the journey moves deeper into North Sikkim as you travel to Lachen and then onward through Chopta Valley to [Gurudongmar Lake](https://indiatour.live/attractions/gurudongmar-lake), one of the highest and most breathtaking lakes in India. The experience continues to Lachung, followed by a visit to Yumthang Valley, known for its wide open landscapes and seasonal beauty.\n\nAfter exploring the raw and remote side of Sikkim, the trip transitions to a more relaxed pace as you travel from Gangtok to Pelling via [Namchi](https://indiatour.live/attractions/namchi). In Pelling, you explore monasteries, waterfalls, and viewpoints including the Skywalk, all set against stunning views of **Kanchenjunga**.\n\nThe final leg takes you to Darjeeling, where the journey ends on a classic note with tea gardens, colonial charm, and the iconic [Tiger Hill](https://indiatour.live/attractions/tiger-hill) sunrise, along with visits to key attractions around the town.\n\nOverall, this [North Sikkim itinerary](https://indiatour.live/tours/north-sikkim-tour-package) is ideal for travelers who want to **experience everything, from high-altitude adventures to peaceful hill stations**, all in one well-paced and immersive trip.\n\n### **Experience North Sikkim** Trip Highlights\n\n#### 🌆 Gangtok\n#### \nIn Gangtok, the highlight is the excursion to **Tsomgo Lake**, a stunning high-altitude lake surrounded by mountains. You’ll also visit Baba Mandir, a revered site dedicated to Baba Harbhajan Singh, making it one of the key experiences of your Gangtok stay.\n\n#### 🏔️ Lachen & Gurudongmar Lake\n#### \nAs you head towards North Sikkim, the journey becomes more raw and scenic. En route to Lachen, you’ll visit Naga Waterfall, Bhim Nala Waterfall, and the confluence of Lachen Chu and [Lachung Chu](https://indiatour.live/attractions/lachung) rivers at Chungthang.\n\nFrom Lachen, you travel through Thangu Valley and continue to Gurudongmar Lake—one of the highest lakes in the world, offering a surreal high-altitude experience unlike anywhere else.\n\n#### 🌄 Lachung & [Yumthang Valley](https://indiatour.live/attractions/yumthang-valley)\n#### \nFrom Lachung, you’ll visit Yumthang Valley, also known as the “Valley of Flowers,” with wide open meadows, grazing yaks, and seasonal blooms.\n\nOn the way back, you’ll stop at the natural Hot Springs, known for their sulfur-rich waters. The return journey to Gangtok also includes scenic stops like Singhik Viewpoint, offering panoramic views of **Kanchenjunga**.\n\n#### 🏞️ Pelling\n#### \nYour Pelling sightseeing includes [Darap Village](https://indiatour.live/attractions/darap-village), Rimbi Waterfalls, Khecheopalri Lake, and Khangchendzonga Waterfalls, offering a mix of nature and culture.\n\nYou’ll also explore [Pemayangtse Monastery](https://indiatour.live/attractions/pemayangtse-monastery) and Rabdantse Ruins, along with panoramic viewpoints like the Skywalk and Helipad Ground, all set against breathtaking Himalayan backdrops.\n\nEn route, you’ll visit Namchi, covering Siddheshwar Dham (Char Dham complex) and Sai Temple.\n\n#### 🌄 Darjeeling\n#### \nDarjeeling covers a blend of iconic viewpoints and cultural attractions. Start early with the Tiger Hill sunrise, where you can witness **Kanchenjunga** in golden light.\n\nYour Darjeeling sightseeing includes the Himalayan Mountaineering Institute, P.N. Zoological Park, Tenzing Rock, and the Darjeeling Ropeway for panoramic views. You’ll also visit the Tibetan Refugee Self-Help Centre, Japanese Temple, Peace Pagoda, and enjoy views of the tea gardens, with evenings free at [Chowrasta](https://indiatour.live/attractions/mall-road-darjeeling) and Mall Road.\n\n**Book Your Complete [North Sikkim Experience](https://indiatour.live/tours/experience-north-sikkim) Now.**\n\n### Why Choose This North Sikkim Package\n\n- Covers **Lachen, Lachung, and Gurudongmar Lake**, which many itineraries skip.\n- Designed as a **complete Sikkim circuit**, not just a standard trip.\n- Perfect for travelers looking for **high-altitude and offbeat experiences**.\n- Combines **adventure with comfort destinations like [Pelling](https://indiatour.live/attractions/pelling) and Darjeeling**.\n- Ideal for travelers who want to explore **North Sikkim in depth**.\n- Private tour ensures flexibility and a well-managed journey.\n\n### Important Travel Tips for North Sikkim Trip\n\n- Carry **heavy woollens**, as temperatures drop significantly in Lachen and Lachung.\n- Be prepared for **long travel hours and changing road conditions**.\n- Stay hydrated and avoid sudden physical exertion at high altitudes.\n- Carry basic medicines, especially for altitude-related discomfort.\n- Follow all permit and local travel guidelines strictly.\n- Keep buffer time in case of weather-related changes.\n\n**Want a Customized [North Sikkim](https://indiatour.live/tours/north-sikkim-tour-package) Experience.**\n\n👉 **Speak to our travel expert and design your [Sikkim trip](https://indiatour.live/tours/sikkim-tour-package/enquiry) your way.**",
