      "overviewText": "This **10 Days 9 Nights North Sikkim tour package with Darjeeling** is a **complete Himalayan journey**, covering Darjeeling, [Pelling](https://indiatour.live/attractions/pelling), Gangtok, and [North Sikkim](https://indiatour.live/tours/best-of-sikkim-darjeeling-with-kalimpong) in one well-paced itinerary.\n\nYour trip begins in [Darjeeling](https://indiatour.live/attractions/darjeeling), where you ease into the mountains with classic hill station charm. The experience includes the iconic Tiger Hill sunrise with views of **Kanchenjunga**, along with visits to key attractions around the town.\n\nFrom here, you travel to Pelling, where the landscapes open up and the Himalayas feel closer. Your Pelling sightseeing includes monasteries, waterfalls, and panoramic viewpoints, along with the Skywalk experience set against stunning mountain views.\n\nThe journey continues to Gangtok via Namchi, followed by an excursion to **[Tsomgo Lake](https://indiatour.live/attractions/tsomgo-lake)** and Baba Mandir—one of the most memorable high-altitude experiences in Sikkim.\n\nAs you move further into [North Sikkim](https://indiatour.live/tours/north-sikkim-tour-package), the trip becomes more raw and adventurous. You travel to Lachung and visit the breathtaking Yumthang Valley, known for its untouched landscapes and seasonal blooms, before returning to Gangtok.\n\nOverall, this North Sikkim Darjeeling itinerary is perfect for travelers who want to **experience everything—from popular highlights to remote Himalayan beauty**, all in one seamless and immersive journey.\n\n### **North Sikkim Tour Package** Highlights\n\n#### 🌄 Darjeeling\n#### \nDarjeeling sightseeing brings together iconic viewpoints and cultural experiences. Start early with the Tiger Hill sunrise, where you can witness **Kanchenjunga** glowing in the morning light.\n\nYou’ll visit the Himalayan Mountaineering Institute, P.N. Zoological Park, and [Tenzing Rock](https://indiatour.live/attractions/tenzing-rock-hmi), along with enjoying panoramic views from the Darjeeling Ropeway. The experience also includes the Tibetan Refugee Self-Help Centre, Japanese Temple, [Peace Pagoda](https://indiatour.live/attractions/japanese-peace-pagoda), and scenic views of the tea gardens, with evenings free at Chowrasta and Mall Road.\n\n#### 🏔️ Pelling\n#### \nPelling offers a mix of nature, culture, and panoramic Himalayan views. Your sightseeing includes Darap Village, Rimbi Waterfalls, Khecheopalri Lake, and Khangchendzonga Waterfalls.\n\nYou’ll also explore Pemayangtse Monastery and Rabdantse Ruins, along with viewpoints like the Skywalk and Helipad Ground, all set against stunning mountain backdrops.\n\nEn route, you’ll stop at [Namchi](https://indiatour.live/attractions/namchi) to visit Siddheshwar Dham (Char Dham complex) and Sai Temple, adding a spiritual touch to the journey.\n\n#### 🌆 Gangtok & North Sikkim\n#### \nIn Gangtok, the highlight is the excursion to **[Tsomgo Lake](https://indiatour.live/attractions/tsomgo-lake)**, a beautiful high-altitude lake, followed by a visit to Baba Mandir.\n\nAs you head towards North Sikkim, the journey becomes more raw and scenic. En route to Lachung, you’ll visit Naga Waterfall, [Bhim Nala Waterfall](https://indiatour.live/attractions/bhim-nala-waterfall), and the confluence of [Lachen Chu](https://indiatour.live/attractions/lachen) and Lachung Chu rivers at Chungthang.\n\n#### 🌸 Yumthang Valley\n#### \nThe North Sikkim experience continues with a visit to Yumthang Valley, known as the “Valley of Flowers,” surrounded by snow-capped peaks and open meadows.\n\nOn your return, you’ll stop at the natural Hot Springs, known for their sulfur-rich waters and therapeutic properties—making it a unique highlight of the trip.\n\n**Book Your [North Sikkim Trip Now](https://indiatour.live/tours/north-sikkim-tour-package).**\n\n### Why Choose This North Sikkim Package\n\n- Covers **[Darjeeling](https://indiatour.live/attractions/darjeeling), Pelling, Gangtok, and North Sikkim** in one trip.\n- Perfect mix of **popular destinations and offbeat experiences**.\n- Ideal for travelers looking for a **complete Himalayan journey**.\n- Includes **North Sikkim**, which is often missed in shorter trips.\n- Multiple stay options available from Basic to Luxury.\n- Private tour ensures comfort, flexibility, and a better travel experience.\n\n### Important Travel Tips for North Sikkim Trip\n\n- Carry **heavy woollens**, especially for Lachung and Yumthang Valley.\n- Keep valid ID proof handy for permits and hotel check-ins.\n- Start early for long travel days in North Sikkim.\n- Carry cash as ATMs are limited in remote regions.\n- Stay hydrated and allow your body to adjust to higher altitudes.\n- Follow local guidelines as North Sikkim is an eco-sensitive region.\n\n**Want a Customized North Sikkim Trip Instead.**\n\n👉 **Talk to our travel expert and plan your [North Sikkim trip](https://indiatour.live/tours/sikkim-tour-package/enquiry) exactly the way you want.**",
